# The Genie screen's prizes (GenieScreen, 80:A63B, its jump table at
# 80:AA6A by the slot the wheel stops on). Played as
# cov_scene_land_figure.box plays to the screen (act 1 stage 0's end with
# $036C set), 120 frames longer; then B starts the wheel, B again 120
# frames on stops it, and it slows and stops by itself about 305 frames
# later; in the $20 frames it waits after (80:AA35, which reads none of
# them) the wheel's angle ($00A8) is set to a slot's (the bounds at
# $80:DA96: 0B 2F 57 81 A9 D3 F9), so the prize read at 80:AA4E is that
# slot's. One pass each: $05 (a lamp: health top $0365 up, GenieHealthFill),
# $05 with $0365 $0A and the gems $0364 $63 (the lamp's 3 gems, stopping
# at 100), $20, $90 and $E0 (a continue, slots 1, 4, 6), $70 (slot 3: health
# at its top, a gem), $70 with health $0367 2 (health filled), $C0 (2
# gems), $FC (past the last bound: slot 0), $40 (slot 2: a gem; then 1200
# frames, to the screen's end and TaskExec). Three more passes set the
# wheel's state at a frame boundary in its stopping loops: 100 frames
# after the second B (slowing, 80:A976) its speed ($00A5) 0, so it runs
# out there (80:A993); 850 frames after (stopping, 80:AA07) its angle 0,
# short of its slot's end (80:AA3F); and there its slot count ($00A9) 1
# with the angle $10 (80:ABF2).
load build/aladdin/states/stage_a1_s0.state
wait 30
poke 001773 00,0B
poke 0019E5 00,0B
poke 0008E7 80,0B
wait 10
poke 001777 00,02
poke 0019E9 00,02
poke 0008EA 80,02
wait 10
poke 001773 00,0F
poke 0019E5 00,0F
poke 001777 00,03
poke 0019E9 00,03
poke 0008E7 80,0F
poke 0008EA 80,03
poke 00036C 01
wait 1720
hold B 4
wait 120
hold B 4
wait 920
poke 0000A8 05
wait 500
